  data: {
    LLM: 'Highest double leads; if no one has a double, redeal. Players then place tiles into the Sevens triangle pattern: doubles progress by adjacent rank on the top row, while non-doubles are placed beneath according to the one-step pip progression pattern. If a player can play, they must play. If not, they draw one tile from boneyard; when boneyard is empty and no play is possible, they pass.',
    Player: 'Highest double leads; if no one has a double, redeal. Players then place tiles into the Sevens triangle pattern: doubles progress by adjacent rank on the top row, while non-doubles are placed beneath according to the one-step pip progression pattern. If a player can play, they must play. If not, they draw one tile from boneyard; when boneyard is empty and no play is possible, they pass.',
    objective: 'Be the first player to domino by playing all tiles.',
    gameplay: 'Highest double leads; if no one has a double, redeal. Players then place tiles into the Sevens triangle pattern: doubles progress by adjacent rank on the top row, while non-doubles are placed beneath according to the one-step pip progression pattern. If a player can play, they must play. If not, they draw one tile from boneyard; when boneyard is empty and no play is possible, they pass.',
    keyRules: [
      'Highest double starts the hand.',
      'If no double is held by any player, redeal.',
      'Must play if able.',
      'Draw from boneyard when blocked; pass only when boneyard is empty.',
    ],
