    turnFlow: 'Highest double leads; if no one has a double, redeal. Players then place tiles into the Sevens triangle pattern: doubles progress by adjacent rank on the top row, while non-doubles are placed beneath according to the one-step pip progression pattern. If a player can play, they must play. If not, they draw one tile from boneyard; when boneyard is empty and no play is possible, they pass.',
